# PR Description in Separate File

When creating Pull Requests, always provide the PR description in a separate markdown file located in `.github/pr-descriptions/` directory, rather than writing it directly in the PR body. This directory is git-ignored to keep draft descriptions out of version control.

## File Naming Convention

Create PR description files with descriptive names using kebab-case:

- `.github/pr-descriptions/separate-publishing-workflow.md`
- `.github/pr-descriptions/fix-track-upload-size-limit.md`
- `.github/pr-descriptions/add-flac-audio-support.md`

## File Structure

Each PR description file should follow the structure from `.github/pull_request_template.md`:

- Description
- Related Issue
- Type of Change
- Target Branch
- Changes Made
- Testing
- Checklist
- Breaking Changes (if applicable)
- Screenshots (if applicable)
- Additional Notes

## Usage

1. Create the PR description file in `.github/pr-descriptions/` with a descriptive name
2. Write the full PR description in that file following the PR template structure
3. When creating the GitHub PR, copy the content from the file
4. The file remains local and git-ignored (not committed to version control)

## Benefits

- **Draft management**: Work on PR descriptions without committing them
- **Organization**: Keep PR descriptions organized locally
- **Template compliance**: Ensures PR descriptions follow the template structure
- **Reusability**: Can reference the file when updating PR descriptions
- **Privacy**: Draft descriptions stay local and aren't tracked in git

## Example

Instead of writing the PR description directly in GitHub:

```markdown
# Bad - Writing directly in GitHub PR
## Description
This PR adds...
```

Create a file:

```markdown
# Good - Separate file: .github/pr-descriptions/my-pr.md
## Description
This PR adds...
```

Then copy the content from the file when creating the GitHub PR.

## File Location

All PR description files should be placed in:
```
.github/pr-descriptions/
```

This directory is git-ignored, so files won't be committed to version control.

## Important Notes

- The `.github/pr-descriptions/` directory is git-ignored - files here are not tracked
- Always copy content from the file when creating the PR (don't reference the file in the PR)
- Delete the file after the PR is created if desired, or keep it for reference
- The file serves as a local draft and documentation
